  "final_text": "Both items exist: the dashboard `EFF-87d195a3 Web logs overview` and the rule `EFF-87d195a3 5xx spike`, which is enabled.\n\n**Data exploration.** I could not query the index directly. Elasticsearch isn't reachable on the usual ports, and Kibana's console proxy drops the API key. I worked from the data view's field list instead. The key fields are `@timestamp`/`timestamp`, `clientip`, `bytes`, `response` (text, with `response.keyword`), `url` (`url.keyword`), `host`, `geo.src`, `extension`, and `agent`. I did not confirm the actual status-code values, so the 5xx rule's regexp `5[0-9][0-9]` is untested against real data.\n\n**Dashboard** (`eff-87d195a3-web-logs-overview-6f269106f899`, default time range last 2 years, since the sample data's timestamps may be old):\n- Total requests (count)\n- Unique client IPs (unique count of `clientip`)\n- Total bytes served (sum of `bytes`)\n- Requests over time (line, date histogram on `timestamp`)\n- Requests by response code (bar, top 10 of `response.keyword`)\n- Top URLs by requests (table, top 10 of `url.keyword`)\n\n**Alert rule** (`5b872cba-cef9-4590-86d6-fb0c326e3356`):\n- Type: Elasticsearch query, on `kibana_sample_data_logs`, time field `timestamp`\n- Runs every 1m; window 5m; fires when the count of 5xx requests is greater than 10\n- Query: `response.keyword` matches `5[0-9][0-9]`, filtered to the rule's `{{date_start}}`\u2013`{{date_end}}` window\n- No action connector attached, so it records alerts but sends no notifications\n- Tagged `EFF-87d195a3`\n\nThe rule's status is still \"pending\" because it has not yet completed a run. I did not confirm that it executes without errors. If the sample data's timestamps are older than 5 minutes, the rule will simply not fire.",
